@how own mechanism: Define the VSAT proof-of-concept as testing whether a minimal story-linking capability helps groups understand their shared situation better. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L7 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: 
  Define the VSAT proof-of-concept as testing whether a minimal story-linking
  capability helps groups understand their shared situation better.

  + context: You are defining proof-of-concept to be a single testable claim (in this case, whether minimal story linking helps groups gain shared insight). This does not apply once the linking claim is already validated for the target cohort.

  + IF:
    Individual stories already shine; the missing capability is “story links →
    group insight”.

  + HOWEVER:
    Without a crisp test concept, funding can drift into general improvements.

  + THEN:
    State that the POC will test whether a basic link/propose/confirm/view loop
    yields new insight for cohorts.

  + BECAUSE:
    Narrow scope keeps effort tied to a partner-relevant question.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Draft the one-paragraph concept statement promised in the staging brief.]
    next[Define an apply signal (e.g., no prior evidence for linking outcomes) and a stop signal (e.g., strong prior evidence exists).]
